From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?L=C3=A9onard?= <leonard@synthe.se>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:51:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] wifi: rtw88: usb: Resubmit the RX URBs after a transient
 error

rtw_usb_read_port_complete() resubmits an RX URB only when it completed
without error. After a transient error (-EPROTO, -EILSEQ, -ETIME,
-ECOMM, -EOVERFLOW: a glitch on the bus) it returns the buffer to the
free queue and stops: the URB is not submitted again. Since
rxcb->rx_skb still points to the returned buffer,
rtw_usb_rx_resubmit_work() skips it as well. Each glitch thus loses one
of the RTW_USB_RXCB_NUM (4) RX URBs for good, and after four of them the
device receives nothing until the interface is reset.

On an RTL8812BU behind the EHCI of a BCM7231, this shows as a slow loss
of the access point's beacons (fewer and fewer frames get through)
ending in a beacon loss and a dead link; a monitor interface, which
multiplies the RX traffic, brought it on within the hour.

Resubmit the URB after a transient error, with a rate-limited warning.
After a fatal one (URB killed, device gone), do not, but clear
rxcb->rx_skb so that it no longer points to a buffer of the free queue.

Fixes: a82dfd33d123 ("wifi: rtw88: Add common USB chip support")
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/usb.c | 20 +++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/usb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/usb.c
index 64e1c34..ea1e83a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/usb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/usb.c
@@ -769,20 +769,30 @@ static void rtw_usb_read_port_complete(struct urb *urb)
 		skb_queue_tail(&rtwusb->rx_free_queue, skb);
 
 		switch (urb->status) {
-		case -EINVAL:
-		case -EPIPE:
-		case -ENODEV:
-		case -ESHUTDOWN:
-		case -ENOENT:
 		case -EPROTO:
 		case -EILSEQ:
 		case -ETIME:
 		case -ECOMM:
 		case -EOVERFLOW:
+			/* A transient error on the bus: resubmit, or the URB
+			 * is lost until the next reset.
+			 */
+			dev_warn_ratelimited(rtwdev->dev,
+					     "rx urb status %d, resubmitting\n",
+					     urb->status);
+			rtw_usb_rx_resubmit(rtwusb, rxcb, GFP_ATOMIC);
+			break;
+		case -EINVAL:
+		case -EPIPE:
+		case -ENODEV:
+		case -ESHUTDOWN:
+		case -ENOENT:
 		case -EINPROGRESS:
+			rxcb->rx_skb = NULL;
 			break;
 		default:
 			rtw_err(rtwdev, "status %d\n", urb->status);
+			rxcb->rx_skb = NULL;
 			break;
 		}
 	}
